-- ============================================================================
-- 25: render-replica LIVE — COMPLETE read-set coverage audit (the user's "full wire
-- trace"). Question: are we missing any wire data that goes STALE and drives the
-- outward-pushed stray/glitch parts? Answer derived 2026-06-13 from the live captures
-- side_cap.mcrr (249f) + rot_cap.mcrr (599f), the transpiled render_frame read-set, and
-- the real render_frame.wasm replayed over the reconstructed seed+dyn RAM. NOT guessed.
-- Apply: tools/re_kb/rekb.sh @tools/re_kb/25_replica_live_readset_coverage_audit.surql
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:replica_live_readset_probes SET kind='tool',
  ref='tools/render-replica-poc/audit_mcrr_reconstruct.py + audit_seed_stale_scan.py + audit_pointer_targets.py + audit_replay_probe.mjs',
  note='Read-set coverage audit harness. Reconstructs SEED (static-prefix ram16) and LIVE@frame (seed + the 15 per-frame dyn regions overlaid == exact client RAM) from a captured MCRR, then (a) unions, over all frames, every RAM byte that differs seed->live yet lies OUTSIDE all shipped dyn regions (stale-seed universe); (b) verifies every chased pointer (idxtab=*0x8C2DAD3C, rectab=*0x8C2DAD4C, ggp=*0x8C26823C, per-node GFX1/GFX2 @ node+0x15C/+0x160, descriptor index node+0xDC into 0x8C1F9F9C) is stable and lands inside a shipped region; (c) replays the real render_frame.wasm and bins per-quad screen-X to locate strays. GOTCHA cited: the live MCRR frame header is 12 bytes (FRMx+vframe+taSize) + dynbytes + a 4-byte trailer (stride=16+dynbytes); reading it as a 16-byte header shifts every region +4 and FALSELY corrupts the tab_ptr/ggp_ptr pointers — that +4 was a reconstruction artifact, NOT a wire bug.';

UPSERT source:replica_live_strays_capture SET kind='live_capture',
  ref='tools/render-replica-poc/{side_cap,rot_cap}.mcrr (MAPLECAST_REPLICA_LIVE state-only stream, 15 dyn regions incl objpool)',
  note='Live replica-live captures with two fighters on screen and a tag-in. rot_cap frame1 slot-walk: L5=node 0x8C2688E4 (P2C1) sid77 anchorX=606 GFX2=0xC8FB8C0 [static-covered]; L6=node 0x8C268E88 (P1C2) sid40 anchorX=35 GFX2=0xC673F60 GFX1=0xC570040 [NOT static-covered]. At CONNECT (seed slot-walk) only P1C1 (0x8C268340, GFX2 0xC52C380) + P2C1 (0x8C2688E4, GFX2 0xC8FB8C0) were active; P1C2 (0x8C268E88) was active=0 -> its GFX was never shipped as a fresh static region.';

-- ---- CONFIRMED: the read-set is FULLY COVERED for resident state; the strays are a
-- ---- STATIC-ONCE GFX gap for a body that was INACTIVE at connect (tag-in). ----
UPSERT finding:replica_live_readset_coverage_audit SET
  statement='COMPLETE render_frame read-set vs shipped wire, audited on two live multi-object captures (side_cap 249f, rot_cap 599f). RESULT: (1) STALE-SEED UNIVERSE IS EMPTY — across every frame, ZERO RAM bytes ever change between the connect-time seed and any live frame OUTSIDE the 15 shipped dynamic regions (audit_seed_stale_scan.py). So NO fixed-address field that render_frame reads goes stale; the dyn set (slot_cn/slot_pt/char_st/objpool/arena/tiledesc/cam_mat/camZ/ggp_ptr/ggp_acc/rparam/tab_ptr/rmode/idxtab/rectab) fully covers all moving resident state. (2) ALL CHASED POINTERS ARE STABLE + COVERED — idxtab=*0x8C2DAD3C=0x8C24B65C and rectab=*0x8C2DAD4C=0x8C24D7DC are constant for the whole match and equal the shipped idxtab/rectab region addrs; ggp=*0x8C26823C=0x8C268240 (ggp_acc, shipped); every body node GFX1/GFX2 base and every descriptor index (node+0xDC into 0x8C1F9F9C) lands inside a shipped region (audit_pointer_targets.py: 0 uncovered, 0 overflow). render_frame reads NOTHING outside the 16MB seed + 15 dyn regions. (3) THE STRAYS ARE NOT A MISSING FIXED-ADDRESS WIRE FIELD — they are the STATIC-ONCE GFX GAP (re_kb finding:replica_live_static_gfx_gap) firing on a TAG-IN body. The server ships fresh GFX1/GFX2 ONLY for the bodies ACTIVE in the slot table at prefix-build (connect): in these captures P1C1+P2C1. The live match renders P1C2 (slot L6, node 0x8C268E88), which was active=0 at connect -> its GFX1(0xC570040)/GFX2(0xC673F60) were NEVER shipped fresh and are served ONLY from the frozen 16MB ram16 seed. The transpiled walker (loc_8c0344d4, gen_walker.c) reads its ENTIRE geometry — cell count + 8B records [dx][dy][flags][sel@+6] + per-sel GFX1 tile-dim/offset — from that stale GFX, so the wide-part tile loop runs with wrong dims/counts and the cumulative pen marches tiles OFF-SCREEN as regular columns/grids.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-13';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_stray_field_pin SET
  statement='THE EXACT STALE FIELD behind the outward strays: the GFX1 tile-dim/offset table + GFX2 cell-record table of any body whose slot was INACTIVE at static-prefix build, read by the walker from the frozen ram16 seed. PINNED on rot_cap.mcrr frame1: render_frame emits 92 quads; q0..q44 = body L5 P2C1 (GFX static-covered, clusters x=512..672, geometry healthy), q45..q91 = body L6 P1C2 (node 0x8C268E88, GFX NOT covered). EVERY L6 quad has per-quad sel=0 and the screen-X forms regular columns/grids at x in {139,114,87,61,34,7,-19,-46,-73} and {111,57,4,-49} marching LEFT off-screen — the user-reported far-LEFT vertical column of fragments. The P1C2 GFX2 cell stream (cellCount=13, sels 120..132) decodes structurally but the per-sel GFX1 part records yield wide-part dims (e.g. sel124 m=10 w=4112 h=17408) that drive an enormous tile loop; the cursor pen (node+0xDC + arena_base + k) then lays the tiles across the screen. Because the SAME stale-GFX mechanism applies to whichever side tags in, the mirror-image far-RIGHT column appears for a P2-side tag-in. ROOT CAUSE: SERVER static-GFX shipper (maplecast_replica_live.cpp buildTables, the L-loop with `if (rd8(node+0x3)!=0) continue`) only enumerates slot-table-ACTIVE bodies at the ONE-SHOT prefix build; a body that activates later (tag-in / 3rd char) never gets fresh GFX. This is exactly finding:replica_live_static_gfx_gap, now pinned to a concrete tag-in node with the stray quads enumerated.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-13';

UPSERT finding:replica_live_readset_fix_priority SET
  statement='PRIORITIZED regions to ADD to the freshly-shipped read-set (the fixes that follow this trace). P0 (causes the visible strays): ON-CHANGE DYNAMIC GFX per ACTIVE body — already specified as finding:replica_live_static_gfx_fix option (a): each frame walk the slot table, for every cat==0 body node read GFX1(+0x15C)/GFX2(+0x160); if a base is not covered by the shipped static GFX regions OR its content changed since last ship, emit that body GFX1+GFX2 (page-aligned, ~121KB zstd) as a tagged DYNAMIC region ONLY on (re)load frames (~0 steady state). This fixes BOTH the geometry (walker cell records) AND the texture decode (client body_decoder reads the same GFX). It supersedes the connect-time-only static GFX. NOTHING ELSE is missing: the fixed-address resident read-set is provably complete (stale universe = 0 bytes) and every chased pointer is covered. P2 (benign / not a stray cause, leave as-is): the cat 1..4 satellite EFFECT path is a CLIENT dispatch stub (finding:replica_live_effect_path_stub) — body-sprite satellites do not yet render, but that is a MISSING render, not a stray, and is not driven by a stale wire field (the objpool dyn region already ships their state, validated 0.00px). No new server read-set region is required for it.',
  status='proposed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-13';

RELATE finding:replica_live_readset_coverage_audit->cites->source:replica_live_readset_probes;
RELATE finding:replica_live_readset_coverage_audit->cites->source:replica_live_strays_capture;
RELATE finding:replica_live_stray_field_pin->cites->source:replica_live_strays_capture;
RELATE finding:replica_live_stray_field_pin->about->finding:replica_live_static_gfx_gap;
RELATE finding:replica_live_readset_fix_priority->cites->source:replica_live_cpp;
RELATE finding:replica_live_readset_fix_priority->about->finding:replica_live_static_gfx_fix;
